# Expo Router Rules

## Route groups
- `(auth)/` — unauthenticated: Welcome, Signin, Signup, Forgot
- `(main)/Business/` — authenticated business app
- Auth gate: `app/index.tsx` redirects on `auth_token` + `isVerifiedEmail`

## Layout files
- `app/_layout.tsx` — root providers only (Redux, Paper, Portal, Toast, Keyboard, Splash)
- Group `_layout.tsx` files configure Stack/Tabs for that segment
- Keep `headerShown: false` unless explicitly needed

## Route file conventions
- File name: `index.tsx` inside feature folders (`Signin/index.tsx`)
- Default export arrow component matching folder purpose
- No business logic beyond routing, redirects, and step orchestration

## Navigation
```ts
import { useRouter, Redirect } from 'expo-router';

router.replace('/(main)/Business/Home');
router.push('/(auth)/Signup');
return <Redirect href="/(auth)/Welcome" />;
```

## Multi-step in routes
- Compose steps with `useMultistepForm([<Step1 />, <Step2 />], { animated: true })`
- Import steps from `@steps/Auth/...` or `@steps/main/Business/...`
- Background gradients/wrappers stay in route file; step content in `@steps/`
